The solution exploits the mathematical property that rotatable numbers of length n in base b relate to the prime n+1. When n+1 is prime, by Fermat's Little Theorem, for any b not divisible by n+1, b^n ≡ 1 (mod n+1), ensuring b^n - 1 is divisible by n+1. This allows construction of rotatable numbers.

